  m_Name: Slide_47_Mech_AiPipeline
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Project.Runtime::DumyatRuntime.TextSlideSO
  _sectionNumber: 6
  _sectionName: Mechanics
  _title: "Merchant AI \xB7 the pipeline"
  _kicker: "Voice in, a haggle, voice out \u2014 with the money kept out of the model's
    hands."
  _speakerNotes: 
  _titleEffects: 0
  _kickerEffects: 0
  _background: {fileID: 0}
  _transitionIn: {fileID: 0}
  _layout: 3
  _posterTreatment: 0
  _body: 
  _bullets:
  - Consent, then the microphone. Voice is opt-in, and a missing headset permission
    is explained on the merchant's subtitle rather than failing silently.
  - Speech to text. Munsit streams the player's Egyptian Arabic over a WebSocket
    and returns one final transcript per utterance.
  - 'One LLM call per turn returns three things: the merchant''s spoken line, the
    action to take, and two scores for what the player meant.'
  - "The money stays deterministic. PriceNegotiationCalculator owns the opening offer,
    the per-turn deception roll and the final score \u2014 the model only colours
    the tone."
  - Intent is measured, never matched. Accepting and declining come from a scored
    judgment against a threshold, because Egyptian-Arabic transcripts are far too
    noisy for keyword checks.
  - Nothing closes on a single turn. An accept or a decline has to be confirmed on
    the next one, or the validator coerces it back into haggling.
  - Text to speech. ElevenLabs voices the reply while the subtitle carries the Arabic
    with an English line beneath it.
  _readouts: []
